File Index

/areas.test.ts
Purpose: Route tests both gate states: listing/preview/diff/download, script + dangling-vnum 400s, atomic save with backup, reload signals, new-area creation (area.lst registration, overlap 400, duplicate 409), header range guards (shrink/overlap 400s, rename saves), Phase 11 conditional saves (baseHash 409 with disk untouched) and world-index ref resolution with live cache invalidation.

/areas.ts
Purpose: Area REST API — list/get(+baseHash)/preview(diff+scripts+refs incl. resolved external links)/download/save plus POST /api/areas new-area creation (copyover-flagged); optional baseHash makes PUT conditional (409 {error,currentHash}); scripts + vnum-ref + header-range validation 400s before disk; no error escapes a handler.

/audit-view.test.ts
Purpose: GET /api/audit tests via full registerRoutes: empty-before-any-mutation, anonymous 401 / API-key 403, newest-first order + ?limit, unparseable line degrades to { raw }.

/audit-view.ts
Purpose: GET /api/audit (Phase 10) — master-only, read-only tail of backups/audit.log (newest first, default 100 / cap 500); missing file = empty, bad line = { raw }; never truncates the log. Takes an introspectConfig param passed straight through to requireMaster (2026-07-24) so an account actor gets the same 403-not-401 treatment here as under /api/auth.

/auth.test.ts
Purpose: Guard + lifecycle tests via full registerRoutes: first-run key gen, 401/403 matrix, create→use→rotate→revoke, master rotation, per-install uniqueness, guard-off mode, corrupt-file lockdown, audit lines without secrets. Phase 4 block: introspect fallback against a fake auth-server (local-first no-network-call proof, unconfigured no-op, valid/invalid/unreachable/hanging/bad-key-path cases, plus a regression case proving requireMaster/GET /api/auth/keys also falls back — an account actor gets 403 not 401). Phase 15 case: a fake introspect response carrying username/expiresAt/tokenType flows through to the audit line as `account:id (label) [username]`. Phase 15/G "requireRebuildAllowed" block (retargeted Phase G from a username allowlist to RoleStore tiers — see routes/roles.test.ts for the store's own grant/ceiling matrix): anonymous 401s, master always passes regardless of role grants, a local API key 403s outright, admin-tier+short-expiry passes, owner-tier also passes, admin-tier+no-expiry (forever key) 403s, admin-tier+too-far-out expiry 403s, no local grant (defaults to user tier) 403s, manager-tier (below admin) 403s.

/auth.ts
Purpose: Phase 9 access guard — authGuard middleware (non-GET /api/* requires a valid bearer) + master-only /api/auth key-management routes (list/create/rotate/revoke, rotate-master); plaintext tokens only in create/rotate responses; exports requireMaster for the audit viewer. Phase 2 (centralized auth service) adds GET /api/auth/introspect-check?token=... — additive proof that a real /api/introspect call against auth-server works, reusing this same master-only mount rather than a new guard (this route echoes the raw IntrospectResult, so Phase 15's username/expiresAt/tokenType fields appear here automatically, no route change needed). Phase 4: authGuard falls back to introspect() (bounded ~3s timeout) for any token the local store misses, producing a BuilderActor{kind:'account'} — local-store tokens are checked first and never touch the network. requireMaster now takes the SAME introspectConfig and falls back too (2026-07-24 fix): before, an introspection-valid account actor landed in requireMaster's bare 401 bucket instead of the 403 "not master" bucket, which mud-builder-client's AccessPage status probe (GET /api/auth/keys) reads as "token REJECTED" even though the key worked everywhere else. Phase 15: tryIntrospect() also threads username/expiresAt from the introspect response into the constructed BuilderActor; adds requireRebuildAllowed — a sibling to requireMaster, mounted on POST /api/rebuild (Step 7) — and extracted the shared local-verify-then-introspect-fallback logic (previously duplicated 3x) into `resolveActor()`, plus `requireAnyActor` (any recognized actor) for GET /api/rebuild/status. Phase G: tryIntrospect() also threads globalRole (hub-global tier) into the BuilderActor — didn't exist before despite introspect always having returned it. `checkRebuildEligibility`/`requireRebuildAllowed` RETARGETED from a `ReadonlySet<string>` username allowlist to a `RoleStore` lookup (admin tier or above via SERVICE_TIERS' tierRank) — the short-lived-token (≤7 days) requirement is unchanged, only the eligibility test itself changed. See routes/roles.ts for the new role-management surface this feeds. Simulacrum plan (2026-08-16): SERVICE_TIERS gained a new `builder` tier between `manager` and `trusted`; authGuard now also takes a RoleStore and, after the identity check, floors every non-GET /api/* mutation at `builder`+ (TIER_CHECK_EXEMPT_PATHS — currently just `/api/presence`, a non-persisting heartbeat — exempts the TIER check only, never the identity check, so an anonymous heartbeat still 401s). `checkRebuildEligibility`'s threshold also dropped from `admin` to `builder` to match. Same-day live bug, found via a user report: that new blanket floor ALSO caught `POST /api/roles/:accountId`, which broke Decision 4's hub-owner bootstrap entirely — a hub owner with no pre-existing local grant (the floor's default) got 403'd before roles.ts's own `canGrant()` (which already has the correct hub-owner-bootstrap exception) ever ran. Fixed by adding `/api/roles` to `TIER_CHECK_EXEMPT_PATHS` — `canGrant()` is now the sole authority for that one surface, same fails-CLOSED reasoning as the presence exemption. (Briefly needed a separate prefix-matching exemption set while the grant route still carried the target accountId as a path segment; folded back into the one exact-match set the same day once that segment moved into the request body as part of the username-based grant redesign — see roles.ts's own note.)

/codegen.test.ts
Purpose: /api/codegen tests: empty GET on missing file, 401 write gate, 400 invalid spec + stock-name collision, save emits an audit line, 409 stale baseHash, text/plain patch download content, unknown-funName 404.

/codegen.ts
Purpose: New-spell codegen API (Phase 14a) — GET /api/codegen/spells (open, {specs, baseHash}), gated+audited PUT (every spec re-validated via validateSpellSpec against stock + live skills.dat overlay names, 400 on any error), GET /api/codegen/spells/:funName/patch (open, regenerates the 4-section C patchText on the fly as text/plain, 404 unknown). Specs are builder metadata only — the game never reads spells.json; deployment stays human.

/groups.test.ts
