/skills.ts
Purpose: skills.dat REST API (Phase 7) — GET (overlay or stock fallback, +baseHash), POST preview, gated PUT (optional baseHash → conditional, 409 carries currentHash; exports readBaseHash shared with groups) with copyover note, DELETE (revert to compiled table); same never-crash safe() contract as areas.

/snippets.test.ts
Purpose: Phase G route tests: 401 anonymous, 403 master/local-key (no accountId to own snippets under), empty list for a fresh account, isolation proof (never sees another account's snippets), PUT round-trip, whole-collection replace (delete-by-omission), 400 malformed entry, 200-item cap enforced.

/snippets.ts
Purpose: Phase G whole-collection GET/PUT /api/snippets over a builder's private Room/Mob/Object/Script templates (snippet-store.ts), keyed by accountId — `kind:'account'`-only (master/key actors 403, not a silently empty list, so the client can tell "not for you" from "you have none yet"). No per-item routes; the client mutates its own copy of the array and PUTs the whole thing back. Simulacrum plan (2026-08-16): registerSnippetRoutes now takes a RoleStore and adds a `requireTrustedAccount` floor (trusted tier or above) — this is the "can draft private content but can't touch real area files" middle rung between the wide-open GETs elsewhere and the new `builder`+ floor on the real persist path (see routes/auth.ts).

/spawn.test.ts
Purpose: GET /api/areas/:file/spawn tests: an M/E/G-style chain (guard wielding a local sword) plus a cross-area P (a local chest holding an object whose template is only defined in a neighbor area) proving the real worldVnumIndex resolver is wired in, not just a local lookup; a broken neighbor file in area.lst doesn't break a healthy file's spawn preview; requesting spawn for the broken file itself 400s (parse error) rather than 500ing; 404/400 filename guards.

/spawn.ts
Purpose: Read-only spawn preview (Phase 13) — GET /api/areas/:file/spawn runs merc-area's simulateResets over the parsed on-disk model with worldVnumIndex wired as the cross-area resolver; mirrors routes/areas.ts's `safe()` error taxonomy (AreaStoreError→its status, ParseError→400, else 500) rather than map.ts's simpler one, since a parse failure must 400 here.

/state.test.ts
Purpose: State route tests via a full registerRoutes app + temp dir: GET with no snapshot -> 404 and creates nothing; POST refresh with no bearer -> 401 and writes nothing; POST refresh with master writes state.request and dedups a second call (pending request untouched, not overwritten); GET 200s with {snapshot, ageMs} once a snapshot file exists (simulating the game having written one); a torn/malformed snapshot -> 404 not a crash; refresh does NOT grow audit.log; refresh 403s when MUD_WRITE_ENABLED is off.

/state.ts
Purpose: Live-state bridge (Phase 14c) — POST /api/state/refresh writes "state.request" into the area dir (same file-handshake shape as reload.signal/copyover.signal, write-gated + dedup'd if one's already pending) so the game's next pulse writes state.snapshot.json; GET /api/state/live reads it back as {snapshot, ageMs} via merc-area's parseLiveSnapshot (a torn/malformed file reads as 404 "no snapshot yet", same as absent — never surfaced as bad JSON). POST is a read trigger, not authoring — excluded from audit.ts; GET stays open (Phase 9).

/world.test.ts
Purpose: /api/world aggregation tests: counts, cross-area warning, and a listed-but-broken file reported instead of dropped.

/world.ts
Purpose: GET /api/world — read-only aggregate over every area.lst entry (header, entity counts, resolver-backed refs: errors, proven-INVALID warnings, resolved external links) plus Phase 12b limitPressure (world-wide spawn demand per mob/object vs the tightest reset limit, db.c decoding, flagged on the defining area); unparseable files stay listed with their parse error.
